{
	title: 'Automatic compaction before the window fills',
	spec: 'Before each provider round the host compares the context used by the last round (input + cache read + cache write) with the model context window; at or above compactAt (fraction, default 0.85; 0 disables it), it compacts between rounds after any tool results and tells the user with a notice. A turn own prompt and every message delivered into that turn remain after its automatic compact boundary, verbatim including images; only preceding context is summarised, even when the boundary is written after the prompt in append-only history. A prompt-too-long refusal (Anthropic wording, OpenAI context_length_exceeded, or 400/413 saying so) compacts and retries the round at most once, then fails with the provider message instead of temporary retry. Test threshold and first-round compaction with images and a restart, mid-turn tool results, disabled compaction, and too-long retry.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"compact.auto (src/host/compact.ts) runs in turns.runTurn right before each non-held round; compact.retry handles a too-long refusal before the failure/backoff branch and deletes its failure so it is never retried forever. Context used = running turn's latest round (input+cacheRead+cacheWrite), else the last turn_end context, but unknown once a compact/reset follows it; history.forget(id) moves the running turn's round usage into prior on every boundary so a stale context never re-triggers.",
		"compactAt needed a new settings type kind 'number' (min/max, any finite number), next to 'integer'. The notice is a plain output record (slash.output), e.g. 'context 85% full (850 of 1000 tokens): compacted'.",
		"A compact at a turn's first round lands after its prompt, so the prompt reaches the model only inside the summary (verbatim, as one of the last three), and its images are dropped. Compacting before the prompt record would need prompts.ts to check first; not done.",
		'Append-only boundaries can reference original prompt record numbers (compact.keep); provider replay places them after the summary with original image blocks, while summary excludes those records. No duplicate display prompt is written.',
		'The earlier note about first-round image loss describes the old bug, now fixed: keep records are replayed after an automatic boundary and excluded from its summary.'
	],
	needs: [
		'bc'
	]
}
